usage: v2_stream_probe.py [-h] --port PORT --output OUTPUT [--seconds SECONDS]
                          --build-id BUILD_ID
                          [--sample-rate {50000,100000,200000}]
                          --source-commit SOURCE_COMMIT
                          --image-sha256 IMAGE_SHA256 [--expect-disconnect]

One explicitly selected physical stream trial; never flashes or resets a
board. The real serial factory is wrapped only to preserve byte-level traffic.
There is no simulator fallback. Host timestamps are diagnostics, not ADC
timestamps.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --port PORT
  --output OUTPUT
  --seconds SECONDS
  --build-id BUILD_ID
  --sample-rate {50000,100000,200000}
                        Require this nominal CAPS rate before START
  --source-commit SOURCE_COMMIT
  --image-sha256 IMAGE_SHA256
  --expect-disconnect
